;; world/rooms/wrongwater/x-2y7.room
(room
  region: wrongwater
  at: (-2 7)
  title: "Under the Well"
  intent: "you drop onto dry ground, and the water you came through hangs overhead with its surface facing down: a breath"
  bed: (air 0.15 water 0.5 hang 0.35 drone 0.6)
  light: 0.6
  grid:
  ("###############o#########"
   "############### #~~~~~###"
   "####    ####    #~~~~~# #"
   "###                     #"
   "##                      #"
   "#                       #"
   "#                       #"
   "                         "
   "                         "
   "##%  %###################"
   "##%  %###################")
  things: ((ring-stone at: (15 0) overtone: 7 still: 5 radius: 2 listen: (glasswood -2 6 15 9)))
  decor: auto)
;; The drip door is this room's (15,0), on the seam: the floor of a one-cell
;; pit, the Ice Well's (15,10), under its rising drip. A body standing on it
;; stays in the Ice Well, 17 px from the drip, so its stillness counts. It is
;; the stillness door (tasks/harkfell-depths-systems): stand still within
;; two tiles of the drip for five seconds and it sinks. The seam and border
;; checks and the reach checker treat a still: stone as open. Under it, a
;; one-cell shaft (15,1) opens into the room. The landing (row 8) is seven
;; rows under the door: the
;; crack cannot be reached again from here. A small lake hangs in a ceiling
;; pocket east of the crack (17-21, rows 1-2), out of every jump's reach: a
;; picture. East to the Hanging Tarn (rows 7-8); down the rough shaft (3-4)
;; to the Upward Grove, whose rough walls are the climb back.
